# Stops npm from consulting .gitignore when it decides what goes into the package.
#
# WHAT WAS MEASURED (npm 11.16.0, 2026-08-24): with the .gitignore beside this file — which
# ignores `dist/`, because build output does not belong in source control — and with no
# .npmignore at all, `npm pack` STILL included `dist/main.js`. The `files` list in package.json
# won. So this file is not fixing a failure that happens today.
#
# It is here because of what that failure WOULD be. `dist/main.js` is exactly what the `bin`
# entry names, npm's precedence between `files` and `.gitignore` has moved between major
# versions before, and a published version number can never be taken back — so a release that
# ships a command that is not there is permanent. One file removes the question instead of
# tracking the answer. The publish workflow also prints the real file list before publishing,
# so a wrong answer would be visible rather than inferred.
*.tsbuildinfo
